# This is the processing directive for uni-temporal Anchor Modeling in Vertica
#
# The templates are in the Sisula language (docs/SISULA.md) and render the JSON bindings that the
# modeler builds (Generate > JSON bindings). The scripts first in the list prepare the schema that the
# bindings are made from; they run once, before the templates. A line starting with # is not run.
#
# Vertica has no function that returns a table, so only the latest and the now perspectives are made. It has no
# triggers either, and no equivalence (the table says so in SQL/Helpers.js).
SQL/Helpers.js
SQL/NamingConvention.js
SQL/Vertica/NamingConvention.js
SQL/Vertica/derive.js
SQL/Vertica/CreateSchemas.sisula
SQL/Vertica/uni/CreateKnots.sisula
SQL/Vertica/uni/CreateAnchors.sisula
SQL/Vertica/uni/CreateNexuses.sisula
SQL/Vertica/uni/CreateAttributes.sisula
SQL/Vertica/uni/CreateTies.sisula
SQL/Vertica/uni/CreateAnchorPerspectives.sisula
SQL/Vertica/uni/CreateNexusPerspectives.sisula
SQL/Vertica/uni/CreateTiePerspectives.sisula
SQL/Vertica/AddDescriptions.sisula
